WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:06.530
Why can't "The Batman" star Robert Pattinson
stand to see certain fish dishes anymore?

00:00:06.530 --> 00:00:10.410
And was he serious when he said he wasn't
working out in lockdown?

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.860
Keep watching for the details of his regimen.

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:17.239
Batman has been played in a variety of ways
over the years by a wide array of actors,

00:00:17.239 --> 00:00:20.570
from Michael Keaton to Christian Bale to Ben
Affleck.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.660
Then there's the latest to don the batsuit,
Robert Pattinson.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:28.269
Though some seem to have done more than others
before putting on the cape and cowl, there's

00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:33.160
no doubt that every Batman actor had to put
in some work to get in shape before taking

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.160
on the role.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.640
The physical standards for a Batman actor
change from project to project.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.520
If anything, it's become more integral than
ever recently, with every Batman now guaranteed

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:47.710
at least one or two shirtless scenes displaying
Bruce Wayne's obsession with remaining vigilant

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:52.030
in mastering his body and mind to weed out
Gotham's criminal underbelly.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:57.010
For "The Batman," pressure was on for the
typically lean Pattinson to bulk up a bit.

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:01.750
He has revealed that he took some fairly drastic
measures to get in shape for the iconic role.

00:01:01.750 --> 00:01:05.829
In an interview with People magazine, Pattinson
revealed he was on a strict diet that helped

00:01:05.829 --> 00:01:09.229
him physically prepare for the role in only
three months.

00:01:09.229 --> 00:01:12.710
And before shirtless scenes, it got really
extreme.

00:01:12.710 --> 00:01:13.710
He said:

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:18.789
"You just cut down and cut down and cut down
before the couple of scenes with your shirt

00:01:18.789 --> 00:01:21.350
off, and you're counting sips of water."

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:25.770
According to Muscle and Fitness, cutting back
to just sips of water is a strategy that can

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:30.820
be used by bodybuilders and wrestlers trying
to drop weight to make a certain weight class.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:35.310
The 35-year-old Pattinson said "shame" was
his biggest motivator in building his Batman

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:38.869
body, and he was working out before and after
work.

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:44.369
The actor has said his diet was bland too,
with the sight of boiled fish, a key component

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:47.679
of his diet, causing him discomfort today.

00:01:47.679 --> 00:01:49.229
He told On Demand Entertainment,

00:01:49.229 --> 00:01:51.180
"I never want to see--"

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:52.180
"Salad?"

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:56.179
"--a piece of white fish with just lemon on
it.

00:01:56.179 --> 00:01:57.599
Boiled fish."

00:01:57.599 --> 00:02:00.869
Pattinson also had to undergo some fairly
intense physical training.

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:05.109
The actor said his routine included weight
training, boxing drills, military sandbag

00:02:05.109 --> 00:02:07.779
drills, and three to six mile runs.

00:02:07.779 --> 00:02:08.779
He said,

00:02:08.779 --> 00:02:12.880
"It's all about pushing boundaries and building
up to a point where you know you can do justice

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.700
to the physicality required."

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:19.030
The actor added that he drew inspiration from
Marvel stars like Robert Downey Jr. and Chris

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:20.170
Hemsworth.

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:24.140
Pattinson's scheduled training included cardio
to start and then a succession of exercises

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:29.640
that sound fun to nobody, like bicycle crunches
and dumbbell side-bends.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:33.970
The physical commitment from Pattinson is
all the more impressive when you consider

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:39.250
how much he hated exercise before the role,
as he's admitted it would have taken a lot

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.300
to get him to do some cardio before "The Batman"
came along.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.300
He joked,

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:47.710
"A few years ago, I would have run a mile
from anything with a physical edge."

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:51.590
"Training's a lot more fun…it's a lot more
fun when you kind of get good at it."

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:55.760
The actor appears to think it was all worth
it — and not just because the film seems

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.650
to be doing well with audiences and critics.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:01.980
He told People that wearing the batsuit on
set was like "wearing a crown or something,"

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:02.980
adding,

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.720
"People react to you differently, the crew
reacts differently.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.300
Your entire world suddenly changes."

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:13.100
Pattinson said fitting into the costume, which
he claimed has an "elemental power to it,"

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:17.580
ended up being an essential part of being
able to buy into the role and accept himself

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.580
in it.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:19.580
He explained,

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:23.430
"It's funny, because you read the script and
you spend loads of time trying to figure out,

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:27.680
'How can I play this character who does these
sort of audacious acts?"

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:32.660
His extensive workout routine and respect
for the Batman myth may come as a comfort

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:37.590
to some fans, as the actor has previously
commented about not working out before "The

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:41.600
Batman," which had some thinking he was not
doing enough to prep for the iconic role.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:45.830
While "The Batman" production was halted due
to the COVID-19 pandemic, Pattinson said that

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:51.350
working out was not a "high priority" for
him, and those working out in quarantine were

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:52.830
"part of the problem."

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:56.700
But Pattinson told MovieMaker his earlier
comments were all in jest.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:58.420
Of course he was staying in shape for the
role.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.420
He said,

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.420
"You're playing Batman.

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.420
You have to work out.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:05.420
I think I was doing the interview when I was
in lockdown, as well, in England...

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:07.520
I was in a lower gear of working out."

